From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:52:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] Apply the tradeability gateway to NSE Scanner V3

Step 4 of the Cross-Scanner Eligibility and Corporate Lifecycle Sprint.

V3 now runs the shared gateway before its own strategy logic, so a symbol that
is not currently tradeable never reaches evaluate_candidate at all.

Changes to v2/orchestrator.py
----------------------------
* market_date is derived from the newest completed session in the universe
  rather than the calendar run date. On a weekend or exchange holiday the run
  date runs ahead of the data, and gating a Sunday run against Sunday would
  mark every symbol stale. Regulatory restrictions are read at the market date
  for gateway purposes for the same reason.
* The gateway runs once over the whole universe before the candidate loop.
  Refusals are converted into EligibilityResult rows, so they flow through the
  existing v3_eligibility_audit table and the existing funnel without a second
  reporting path. Gateway verdicts are additionally persisted to
  tradeability_audit_v3.
* entry_blocked is enforced at position creation: a symbol under an APPROVED
  corporate scheme stays ranked and displayed but cannot open a fresh paper
  position. Terminal symbols are already gone by this point.
* The admin message gains a TRADEABILITY GATEWAY section that names terminal
  symbols with their successor and flags a run date that trails the data.
* DailyRunResult gains market_date, tradeability_funnel and
  entry_blocked_symbols.

Verified against the real CSV store, market date 2026-08-20:

  TRADEABILITY GATEWAY - market date 2026-08-20
  Admitted: 1657 of 2157
  NOT_IN_CURRENT_NSE_UNIVERSE: 265
  NON_EQ_SERIES: 123
  RESTRICTED_SECURITY: 111
  TERMINAL_MERGER: 1
  TERMINAL JBCHEPHARM: TERMINAL_MERGER -> TORNTPHARM
  CORPORATE REVIEW KIRLPNU: entry withheld

Historical replay is unaffected: a run at as_of=2026-07-16 still admits
JBCHEPHARM as TRADEABLE, and its price history is untouched. Both are asserted
in tests/test_v3_tradeability_wiring.py (12 tests).

Suite: 253 passed. The 7 failures in tests/test_institutional_telegram.py,
test_v2_sprint3.py and test_v2_sprint4_processor.py are stale Telegram
copy-text assertions that fail identically on pristine main.

Momentum Ladder and Hull Pine are not wired yet; those are steps 5 and 6.
